WEBVTT

00:02.535 --> 00:05.766
<i>It seems today that all you see</i>

00:05.872 --> 00:09.205
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i>

00:09.309 --> 00:12.608
<i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i>

00:12.979 --> 00:15.504
<i>On which we used to rely?</i>

00:15.749 --> 00:18.775
<i>Lucky there's a family guy</i>

00:19.052 --> 00:22.351
<i>Lucky there's a man who
Positively can do</i>

00:22.455 --> 00:24.082
<i>All the things that make us</i>

00:24.190 --> 00:25.521
<i>Laugh and cry</i>

00:25.892 --> 00:30.761
<i>He's a family guy</i>

00:37.270 --> 00:40.205
Peter, thanks a lot
for having us out on your boat.

00:40.306 --> 00:43.070
- No problem.
- Peter, are you sure Santos and Pasqual...

00:43.176 --> 00:45.736
don't mind coming in on a Saturday
to serve us drinks?

00:45.845 --> 00:47.676
Are you kidding, Lois? They're Portuguese.

00:47.781 --> 00:50.841
Work is their cocaine.
Besides, look at them in their tuxedos.

00:50.950 --> 00:52.417
They look like little people.

00:58.925 --> 01:01.155
Hey, Meg. What's going on?

01:01.261 --> 01:03.126
What's going on? You having a good time?

01:03.229 --> 01:05.459
Yeah, no, I'm having a good time.

01:06.833 --> 01:08.027
Hey, what's going on?

01:09.135 --> 01:12.104
Listen, you're 17 now, right?

01:12.205 --> 01:14.673
I was just throwing it out there.

01:14.774 --> 01:17.368
I was thinking, you know,
if you ever want to...

01:17.610 --> 01:19.544
I don't know, screw around or something.

01:19.646 --> 01:20.977
Hey, Joe.

01:21.981 --> 01:25.314
So, you know, it's just something to mull
around in the old noggin.

01:28.054 --> 01:31.285
Damn. What is it about golf
that always brings out the worst in me?

01:31.758 --> 01:35.956
So, Annika Sorenstam,
you're quite the female golfer, aren't you?

01:36.196 --> 01:38.596
Yes, quite the female golfer.

01:39.566 --> 01:41.932
I knew it! Look! Everybody, look! Look!

01:42.035 --> 01:43.263
She's a fraud!

01:44.170 --> 01:46.263
All right, I caught a fish!

01:47.140 --> 01:50.166
Sorry about that, Loretta.
Hey, can I have my fish back?

01:50.276 --> 01:53.211
You're gonna have to reach
into the cookie jar.

01:53.313 --> 01:57.215
Well, I can't just...
You're my best friend's wife.

01:57.317 --> 01:58.545
Reach into... All right!

01:58.651 --> 02:02.109
Yeah, you go in and get that.
Show that fishy who's boss.

02:02.222 --> 02:06.591
Loretta, they have some of that
three-bean salad you're so fond of.

02:06.693 --> 02:08.388
Hey, Quagmire.

02:09.062 --> 02:11.724
Well, we'll have to do this
again sometime.

02:11.831 --> 02:14.322
You name the time and the place,
little neck.

02:22.041 --> 02:24.134
I've always loved charades.

02:24.244 --> 02:26.906
- Your turn, Joe.
- The category is Famous People.

02:27.013 --> 02:28.947
- Okay, guess who I am.
- Ironside!

02:29.048 --> 02:30.743
- Larry Flynt!
- Stephen Hawking!

02:30.850 --> 02:33.375
- Dr. Strangelove!
- Roy Campanella!

02:33.486 --> 02:35.249
- Richard Petty!
- Lance Armstrong!

02:35.355 --> 02:36.845
Neil Armstrong! Stretch Armstrong!

02:36.956 --> 02:38.947
Stretch Cunningham!
Howard Cunningham! Potsie Weber!

02:44.230 --> 02:46.494
Natalie Wood. Definitely Natalie Wood.

02:46.599 --> 02:49.534
- Somebody save him, he can't swim!
- He's not even kicking.

02:49.636 --> 02:52.070
- Kick, Joe, kick!
- Peter, he's a paraplegic.

02:52.172 --> 02:54.436
That doesn't mean he can't hear.
Kick, Joe, kick!

02:57.510 --> 02:59.171
Somebody help him!

03:03.816 --> 03:05.044
Gay!

03:08.288 --> 03:10.415
You were right, Peter.
It was Natalie Wood.

03:15.828 --> 03:18.729
Lois, why the hell do we have to
take a stupid CPR class?

03:18.831 --> 03:21.800
Because, Peter, none of us knew
what to do when Joe was drowning.

03:21.901 --> 03:23.869
Now, be quiet and pay attention.

03:23.970 --> 03:27.235
Hi, there. I'd like to welcome you all
to CPR.

03:27.574 --> 03:30.008
I see a lot of smiles here in this room.

03:30.109 --> 03:32.873
There's one. There's another.

03:33.112 --> 03:34.477
That's good.

03:34.847 --> 03:38.044
I see that soda up under your chair.
That's all right.

03:38.151 --> 03:42.918
Soda's all right on my watch.
We also got Oreos here and fresh coffee.

03:43.690 --> 03:46.056
Everybody likes a snack.

03:46.159 --> 03:48.457
Now, who wants to go first?

03:48.561 --> 03:51.121
No takers? Well, fine. I'll go first.

03:51.231 --> 03:52.664
Peter, why don't you volunteer?

03:52.765 --> 03:55.393
No, I don't volunteer for anything
since I helped those guys...

03:55.501 --> 03:56.968
repaint the Sistine Chapel.

03:59.305 --> 04:03.503
Listen, I thought the stuff that was there
was kind of lame. So I put this up.

04:03.610 --> 04:05.669
I figured Andre the Giant
would be a little hipper.

04:05.778 --> 04:07.473
Get back some of those boys
you scared away.

04:07.714 --> 04:09.875
And that's pretty much all there is to it.

04:09.983 --> 04:12.577
It's hard, jagged, and tastes like alcohol.

04:12.685 --> 04:14.983
Just like kissing Faye Dunaway.

04:16.322 --> 04:17.380
Easy now.

04:18.224 --> 04:20.590
I can't believe we just did that.

04:20.693 --> 04:24.459
But, you know, that stuff about
spending the day together tomorrow...

04:24.564 --> 04:26.657
I forgot. Actually, I have a thing.

04:26.766 --> 04:29.257
But, you know,
you have my e-mail address.

04:29.369 --> 04:32.031
So drop me a line. And then I'll have yours.

04:32.138 --> 04:35.733
And we'll take it from there. So...

04:38.711 --> 04:40.110
Bellybutton.

04:40.446 --> 04:41.640
Well, I'll see you later.

04:42.015 --> 04:45.143
So, it's official.
Y'all are card-carrying lifesavers.

04:45.251 --> 04:47.481
Holy crap, a card with my name on it!

04:47.620 --> 04:50.714
I am now Peter Griffin, certified CPR.

04:50.823 --> 04:52.848
Come on, Lois! I've got lives to save.

04:52.959 --> 04:54.756
Thanks. Be safe.

04:54.861 --> 04:56.920
Nobody had any of the coffee.

04:57.030 --> 05:00.932
Only a couple of Oreos gone.
I'm gonna take the rest home to the cats.

05:03.903 --> 05:05.837
Sorry, I was dialing the phone.
Are you all right?

05:05.938 --> 05:07.997
Don't worry about it.
Doesn't look like there's any...

05:08.107 --> 05:10.667
Peter Griffin, certified CPR.
Don't anyone panic!

05:11.611 --> 05:14.774
- What the hell are you doing?
- You know, I don't think he's hurt.

05:14.881 --> 05:17.543
I'll get to you in a moment, sir.
I'm gonna have to check...

05:17.650 --> 05:18.878
and see if he soiled himself.

05:18.985 --> 05:21.180
- Sir? Sir?
- What the hell is wrong with you?

05:21.287 --> 05:23.653
- I've got to check if you've soiled yourself.
- Get off of me. Are you crazy?

05:23.756 --> 05:25.690
Sir? I'm gonna need you
to stop struggling, all right?

05:25.792 --> 05:26.850
- Leave him alone.
- I hurt my elbow!

05:26.959 --> 05:29.189
- I've got to get these trousers off.
- Somebody call the cops!

05:29.295 --> 05:32.321
- I gotta see if you soiled yourself.
- Nobody asked you to get involved!

05:32.432 --> 05:33.831
Get off him, you jackass!

05:33.933 --> 05:37.027
I'm gonna need you to step back. All right,
Looks like we're clean down here.

05:37.136 --> 05:40.128
You guys take it easy. No need to
thank me. Just pay it forward.

05:40.406 --> 05:42.931
- So they revoked your CPR card, huh?
- Yeah.

05:43.042 --> 05:45.306
This is worse than
when they took away my library card...

05:45.411 --> 05:46.810
for reading while intoxicated.

05:47.347 --> 05:50.180
Don't be ashamed of your hand,
Johnny Tremain.

05:50.283 --> 05:52.808
You still live in exciting times.

05:52.919 --> 05:53.908
Crap!

05:54.020 --> 05:56.147
Sir, do you know how loud
you were reading?

05:56.255 --> 05:59.349
"The life of a silversmith's apprentice
was not an easy one!"

06:00.426 --> 06:02.724
I got to figure out some way
to get that card back.

06:02.829 --> 06:04.387
You could always take the class again.

06:04.497 --> 06:06.226
I mean, I'm sure they'd give you
another card.

06:06.332 --> 06:07.299
[Screaming]

06:07.433 --> 06:08.764
- Hey, do you hear that?
- What?

06:08.868 --> 06:10.096
Sounds like someone screaming.

06:10.203 --> 06:11.761
What is it, boy?
What are you trying to say?

06:11.871 --> 06:13.168
It sounds like Loretta is screaming.

06:13.272 --> 06:15.103
- Trouble at the old mill?
- What are you, insane?

06:15.208 --> 06:16.698
- Somebody fall through the ice?
- It's summer.

06:16.809 --> 06:18.106
- Bobcat?
- [Barking]

06:18.211 --> 06:20.270
Loretta's in trouble? Come on, boy!

06:21.447 --> 06:23.608
Peter Griffin,
temporarily suspended CPR...

06:23.716 --> 06:26.685
- Holy crap!
- We should go.

06:27.720 --> 06:29.153
Boy, that was embarrassing, huh?

06:29.255 --> 06:31.280
Walking in on Loretta and Cleveland
having sex.

06:31.391 --> 06:33.882
- Peter, that wasn't...
- You know, for a large, heavyset...

06:33.993 --> 06:35.961
black guy,
Cleveland's got a cute, little white ass.

06:36.062 --> 06:37.962
That wasn't Cleveland.
It was some white guy.

06:38.131 --> 06:39.962
- What was that?
- Shut up and put some more...

06:40.066 --> 06:42.057
of that sugar in my bowl.

06:46.406 --> 06:49.603
Wait a minute. Brian? If that wasn't
Cleveland doing it with Loretta...

06:49.942 --> 06:51.739
then Loretta's having an affair.

06:51.844 --> 06:53.175
We can't tell anyone about this.

06:53.279 --> 06:55.713
That is the last thing in the world
we want to do.

06:55.815 --> 06:58.579
What a day!
We've done everything in the world.

06:58.684 --> 07:00.242
So I guess the only thing left to do...

07:00.353 --> 07:02.253
is tell you that Loretta Brown
is having an affair.

07:02.355 --> 07:03.754
- Good Lord!
- Oh, no!

07:03.856 --> 07:05.016
<i>Oh, God! I'm screwed.</i>

07:05.124 --> 07:07.490
<i>This is worse than that time
I had to fess up to the nation.</i>

07:07.794 --> 07:11.787
My fellow Americans,
I have not been entirely truthful with you.

07:11.898 --> 07:14.128
I did ga-googity that girl.

07:14.233 --> 07:17.396
I ga-shmoigedied her ga-flavety
with my googus.

07:17.503 --> 07:18.868
And I am sorry.

07:18.971 --> 07:20.836
Yeah, any idea who it was, Peter?

07:20.940 --> 07:22.498
No, we didn't see his face.

07:22.975 --> 07:24.909
All we know is it's a skinny white guy...

07:25.011 --> 07:26.535
with a tattoo on his left butt cheek.

07:26.646 --> 07:29.774
Well, I better tell Cleveland.
I got a knack for delivering bad news.

07:29.916 --> 07:32.043
I don't know how to tell you this,
Mr. DeVanney.

07:32.151 --> 07:33.516
So I'll let these guys do it.

07:35.254 --> 07:37.119
<i>[Singing] You have AIDS
Yes, you have AIDS</i>

07:37.223 --> 07:40.283
<i>I hate to tell you, boy, that you have AIDS
You've got the AIDS</i>

07:40.393 --> 07:44.625
<i>You may have caught it
when you stuck that filthy needle in here</i>

07:44.730 --> 07:47.756
<i>Or maybe all that unprotected sex
put you here</i>

07:47.867 --> 07:51.030
<i>It isn't clear
But what we're certain of is you have AIDS</i>

07:51.137 --> 07:55.471
<i>Yes, you have AIDS
Not HIV, but full-blown AIDS</i>

07:57.210 --> 08:00.441
<i>Be sure that you see</i>

08:00.546 --> 08:05.279
<i>That this is not HIV</i>

08:06.919 --> 08:10.548
<i>But full-blown AIDS
Not HIV, but really</i>

08:10.656 --> 08:12.647
<i>Full-blown AIDS</i>

08:12.758 --> 08:16.558
<i>I'm sorry
I wish it was something less serious.</i>

08:16.996 --> 08:19.430
<i>But it's AIDS</i>

08:19.532 --> 08:24.265
<i>You've got the AIDS</i>

08:29.342 --> 08:31.173
So, listen, Cleveland.

08:31.277 --> 08:32.938
The reason I asked you out here...

08:33.045 --> 08:35.411
I've been wanting to talk to you
about something.

08:35.515 --> 08:39.042
<i>In Superman II, what is the story
with that cellophane "S"...</i>

08:39.151 --> 08:41.676
that Superman rips off his chest
and throws at the bad guy?

08:43.022 --> 08:45.456
Prepare to be destroyed, Superman!

08:49.462 --> 08:51.657
- What was that?
- Yeah, take that, you jerk.

08:51.764 --> 08:54.289
- That was a minor inconvenience.
- Yeah, well, that's the idea.

08:54.400 --> 08:56.334
- Slowed you down.
- I'll say. Ow.

08:56.435 --> 08:57.959
- Didn't see that coming, did you?
- No.

08:58.070 --> 08:59.765
Yeah, well, you know, take that.

08:59.972 --> 09:01.735
Which actually brings me
to my next point:

09:01.841 --> 09:04.241
- Your wife's cheating on you.
- What?

09:04.343 --> 09:07.471
Yeah, it's actually a pretty funny story,
true story.

09:07.580 --> 09:11.243
Brian and I walked into your house
and she was with some guy going...

09:11.417 --> 09:12.748
Bam, bam, bam.

09:13.920 --> 09:15.854
- Peter, maybe...
- Hang on, I'm not done.

09:15.988 --> 09:16.977
Bam, bam.

09:17.089 --> 09:20.547
And then she's all, "Oh, yeah. Oh, yeah."

09:20.760 --> 09:21.954
Bam, bam, bam.

09:22.094 --> 09:23.652
You want to take it
from here, Bamm-Bamm?

09:23.796 --> 09:25.229
Bam-bam, bam-bam.

09:25.398 --> 09:27.025
- You want to take it from here, Emeril?
- Bam!

09:27.166 --> 09:29.157
So that's what we're dealing with here.
Any thoughts?

09:31.470 --> 09:34.200
Loretta, is it true what they're saying?

09:34.307 --> 09:37.936
Were you really having carnal relations
with another gentleman?

09:38.044 --> 09:41.070
I'm a woman, Cleveland.
I need some passion in my life.

09:41.180 --> 09:44.343
I need a real man.
And Lord knows that ain't you.

09:44.450 --> 09:48.887
Well, I admit after a long day at work,
I don't always come home...

09:48.988 --> 09:53.357
with that "Riunite on ice,
that's nice" mentality.

09:53.459 --> 09:55.324
And for that, I apologize.

09:55.428 --> 09:59.194
Apologize? I cheat on you
and you apologize to me?

09:59.298 --> 10:02.062
Cleveland Brown, you are pathetic!

10:02.168 --> 10:05.228
I disagree, but I respect your candor.

10:05.338 --> 10:07.033
Goodbye, Cleveland.

10:07.707 --> 10:08.696
I love you.

10:09.609 --> 10:10.633
[Doorbell ringing]

10:11.944 --> 10:13.172
Hi, Cleveland.

10:13.279 --> 10:16.248
- Hey, what are you doing here?
- Loretta kicked me out.

10:16.349 --> 10:20.308
Cleveland, I am so sorry.
You can stay here as long as you like.

10:20.486 --> 10:21.976
Cleveland, sit down.

10:22.088 --> 10:26.252
I want to sing a little song
that kept me going when I had troubles.

10:26.525 --> 10:28.459
[Playing Rock Lobster by the B-52's]

10:31.597 --> 10:33.462
<i>[Singing]
We were at the beach</i>

10:34.266 --> 10:36.791
<i>Everybody had matching towels</i>

10:36.902 --> 10:39.234
<i>Somebody went under a dock</i>

10:39.338 --> 10:41.932
<i>And there they saw a rock</i>

10:42.041 --> 10:43.736
<i>But it wasn't a rock</i>

10:44.877 --> 10:47.277
<i>It was a rock lobster</i>

10:52.284 --> 10:53.751
<i>Rock lobster</i>

10:57.623 --> 10:59.090
<i>Rock lobster</i>

11:03.596 --> 11:05.791
Yeah, you're gonna be okay.

11:10.002 --> 11:13.096
Now, everybody, Cleveland's gonna be
staying with us for a few days.

11:13.205 --> 11:15.696
That's right, kids.
So just treat him like one of the family.

11:15.808 --> 11:19.972
You mean like Cousin Janine who we're
polite to but then mock her diabetes...

11:20.079 --> 11:21.706
on the drive home?

11:21.814 --> 11:23.372
She can't eat caramel.

11:24.550 --> 11:25.881
Exactly.

11:25.985 --> 11:27.680
Can I touch your hair?

11:27.787 --> 11:29.914
I'm gonna do it. I'm gonna touch it.

11:30.356 --> 11:31.789
It's like a sheep!

11:33.893 --> 11:36.521
You know, Peter,
I'm a little worried about Cleveland.

11:36.662 --> 11:38.960
His wife cheated on him,
kicked him out of the house...

11:39.065 --> 11:40.498
and he doesn't seem at all affected by it.

11:40.599 --> 11:43.363
He's probably bottling up his emotions.
That's not good for you.

11:43.469 --> 11:46.802
Right. I almost got an ulcer
after you shelled out $200...

11:46.906 --> 11:48.840
<i>for tickets to Crossing Over
with John Edward.</i>

11:48.941 --> 11:51.466
I'm sensing an "A."
Does your name begin with an "A"?

11:51.577 --> 11:52.566
- No.
- A "B"?

11:52.678 --> 11:56.671
- No.
- C, D, E, F, G, H, I, J, K, L, M, N, O, P?

11:56.782 --> 11:59.114
- "P"! Peter! My name's Peter!
- Is your name Peter?

11:59.218 --> 12:01.584
Wow, you are some kind of sorcerer.

12:01.854 --> 12:05.346
What Cleveland really needs right now
is to learn how to express his feelings.

12:05.458 --> 12:08.120
Now, what he needs right now
is a revenge lay.

12:08.227 --> 12:10.525
And I know just who to talk to.

12:15.000 --> 12:16.194
[Doorbell ringing]

12:17.503 --> 12:20.472
- Oh, God!
- Sorry, guys. Let me throw something on.

12:23.542 --> 12:26.443
- Peter, look!
- Holy crap, that's the tattoo!

12:26.545 --> 12:29.514
Well, I think we're about to find out
who the culprit is.

12:29.615 --> 12:31.810
5-5-5-0-1-4-3.

12:31.951 --> 12:34.078
- Peter, l...
- Shut up, Brian! I'm sleuthing.

12:34.186 --> 12:35.153
[Phone ringing]

12:35.254 --> 12:36.380
- Hello?
- Quagmire?

12:36.489 --> 12:37.979
- Yeah.
- Hey, it's Peter.

12:38.090 --> 12:40.388
What's going on, buddy?
We're at your house.

12:40.493 --> 12:42.893
Peter, he's the one we saw
sleeping with Loretta!

12:42.995 --> 12:43.984
Oh, my God!

12:44.096 --> 12:45.393
Damn it, I knew this was gonna happen!

12:45.498 --> 12:47.693
I didn't mean it, you know?
I knew it was a mistake!

12:47.800 --> 12:49.825
It never felt right!
Please don't tell Cleveland!

12:49.935 --> 12:51.926
Well, all right, Quagmire.

12:52.037 --> 12:54.232
Cleveland, Quagmire's sleeping
with your wife!

12:54.340 --> 12:56.865
- What?
- Quagmire slept with Loretta?

12:57.009 --> 13:00.172
Oh, my God, Cleveland! I am so sorry.

13:00.279 --> 13:02.839
I can only imagine
what you must be feeling right now.

13:02.948 --> 13:04.006
It's okay.

13:04.116 --> 13:07.608
It's okay? It's okay to be betrayed
by your wife and best friend?

13:07.720 --> 13:11.850
Better it be Quagmire than someone
she could get a disease from.

13:11.957 --> 13:15.188
Cleveland, don't you see?
This is why your wife left you.

13:15.294 --> 13:17.091
You don't have any passion.

13:17.196 --> 13:19.994
Sometimes a woman wants to see
her man be a man.

13:20.099 --> 13:21.566
You got to push back a little!

13:21.667 --> 13:24.932
You got to get a little rough!
Oh, God! Peter, hit me!

13:25.037 --> 13:26.504
Yeah!

13:28.440 --> 13:32.274
Wow, so that's something,
about Quagmire and Loretta, huh?

13:32.645 --> 13:34.408
Cleveland, we got to get
your manhood back.

13:34.513 --> 13:35.878
Now, the first thing we're gonna do...

13:35.981 --> 13:38.211
is take you to a good, old-fashioned,
wrestling match.

13:40.786 --> 13:43.118
All right, Cleveland.
Nothing like a good smackdown...

13:43.222 --> 13:44.587
to get the testosterone going.

13:44.690 --> 13:48.786
<i>I must be in Quahog
'cause all I see is a bunch of hicks!</i>

13:48.894 --> 13:51.454
You take that back,
Macho Man Randy Savage!

13:51.564 --> 13:52.963
Doesn't he make you so mad you just...

13:53.065 --> 13:54.828
- want to go down there and hit him?
- No.

13:54.934 --> 13:56.424
Well, maybe not him
'cause he's kind of big.

13:56.535 --> 13:58.594
But don't you want to hit the guy
sitting next to you?

13:58.704 --> 14:00.035
Not him 'cause he's kind of big, too.

14:00.139 --> 14:01.697
But don't you want to hit his kid?

14:01.807 --> 14:04.503
Take that, Macho Man Randy Savage.
You jerk.

14:07.012 --> 14:10.948
All right, Cleveland. If this doesn't
light a fire in your belly, nothing will.

14:11.050 --> 14:14.178
Hey, look at me. I'm Quagmire.
I had sex with your wife.

14:17.089 --> 14:19.751
Those are so his mannerisms.

14:20.459 --> 14:23.257
- Peter, what the hell are you doing?
- I'm not Peter, I'm Quagmire.

14:23.362 --> 14:25.592
- And I'm doing you, Loretta.
- What the hell?

14:25.698 --> 14:27.063
- You like that? Yeah.
- Hey!

14:27.166 --> 14:29.134
- Much better than Cleveland.
- Peter, knock it off!

14:29.235 --> 14:31.635
- Get you damn hands off me...
- You like it dirty, don't you?

14:31.737 --> 14:34.228
What the hell are you doing?
What is that in your pocket?

14:34.340 --> 14:36.968
- Lois! Somebody!
- Quagmire's got you. Yeah.

14:38.110 --> 14:41.602
Glenn Quagmire, you're dead!

14:41.847 --> 14:43.474
[Theme music from Popeye]

14:54.426 --> 14:55.950
All right, calm down, Cleveland.

14:56.061 --> 14:58.586
I'm gonna kill Quagmire!

14:58.697 --> 15:01.825
Oh, God, you're hyperventilating!
Chris, get me a bag.

15:01.934 --> 15:04.698
Okay, Cleveland, breathe into the bag.
It'll calm you down.

15:04.803 --> 15:06.737
- Peter, I'm not sure that that's...
- Not now, Lois!

15:06.839 --> 15:09.569
Okay, Cleveland, Cleveland,
relax, relax, relax.

15:09.675 --> 15:10.937
Relax, relax.

15:11.110 --> 15:14.739
There you go. There you go. Okay.

15:14.847 --> 15:16.144
It's okay. It's okay.

15:16.248 --> 15:19.046
- It's all gonna be okay.
- Peter, you better do your CPR.

15:19.151 --> 15:22.120
There's no time. I got to go warn
Quagmire while I got the chance.

15:22.221 --> 15:23.950
Quick, to the Peter copter!

15:29.561 --> 15:30.687
[Peter screaming]

15:32.031 --> 15:34.295
Oh, God! Oh, God! Oh, God! Oh, my God!

15:34.900 --> 15:37.130
- Peter, what the hell?
- Joe, get inside!

15:37.236 --> 15:40.171
- The blades are still spinning!
- Oh, my God, Peter! What is that thing?

15:40.272 --> 15:42.103
- Joe! Get inside!
- It's tearing up my yard!

15:42.207 --> 15:44.437
- Oh, my God!
- No!

15:48.213 --> 15:51.614
- Joe, I am sorry, buddy.
- It's okay. Look, it's okay.

15:51.717 --> 15:54.208
- Are you okay? You all right?
- It's okay. I'm fine.

15:54.320 --> 15:55.981
- Everybody's fine.
- That was scary.

15:58.157 --> 16:00.421
- Peter, what are we doing here?
- Trust me, Quagmire.

16:00.526 --> 16:03.393
Cleveland will never think to look
for you at Mayor West's house.

16:03.495 --> 16:04.462
- Hey, there.
- How you doing?

16:04.563 --> 16:05.587
Good evening, gentlemen.

16:05.698 --> 16:07.928
Listen, Mayor West,
my friend Quagmire here's in trouble.

16:08.033 --> 16:11.969
- He needs a place to stay tonight.
- Say no more. I'll protect you, sir.

16:12.071 --> 16:16.064
It is my job. I only ask
that you do not feed my cat, Bootsie...

16:16.175 --> 16:18.473
as he's already eaten and might throw up.

16:22.514 --> 16:26.314
<i>Well, Derwood, now you really are
the big man of the house.</i>

16:26.418 --> 16:28.352
Mother, change him back.

16:29.421 --> 16:31.912
You know, Endora,
I'm getting a little sick of this crap.

16:32.157 --> 16:34.682
You ever seen one of these? Huh?
You know what this is? Huh?

16:34.793 --> 16:37.159
- No!
- Yeah, it's holy water. Huh? Yeah.

16:37.262 --> 16:39.423
Try it. How's that feel?

16:39.531 --> 16:40.589
You like that?

16:40.699 --> 16:42.257
Power of Christ compels you, bitch.

16:42.568 --> 16:44.126
<i>I hate Bewitched.</i>

16:46.071 --> 16:49.063
Hey, so that's a pretty
reasonable reaction, huh?

16:51.143 --> 16:54.635
It's all right to go to sleep, my friend.
I'll stand guard.

16:54.747 --> 16:56.009
Okay.

16:56.115 --> 16:59.710
Don't worry. I'll be here all night.
Just don't try to make me smile.

16:59.852 --> 17:01.752
I'm forbidden to smile.

17:04.023 --> 17:05.456
Oh, no.

17:05.557 --> 17:08.185
<i>That episode of Growing Pains
when Mike's friend Boner...</i>

17:08.293 --> 17:10.727
ran for student council.

17:10.829 --> 17:11.818
Boner.

17:11.930 --> 17:15.263
His name was Boner.

17:32.618 --> 17:35.382
- I've failed you.
- This is kind of creeping me out.

17:35.487 --> 17:37.614
- I'm gonna go.
- Take this, for protection.

17:37.723 --> 17:38.747
What the hell's this for?

17:38.857 --> 17:41.951
When the time comes, you'll know.

17:43.162 --> 17:45.960
I'll teach him to mess with my wife.

17:46.065 --> 17:49.262
Hi, Cleveland.
Will you be joining us for dinner?

17:49.468 --> 17:50.435
[Cleveland growls]

17:50.769 --> 17:53.567
- Okay, then.
- He's a Rocky machine!

17:54.339 --> 17:56.534
Peter, we have got to do something
about Cleveland.

17:56.642 --> 17:58.269
I think you created a monster.

17:58.377 --> 17:59.935
Well, there's only one thing to do, Lois.

18:00.045 --> 18:02.513
We've got to get
Loretta and Cleveland back together.

18:02.648 --> 18:06.049
And I know just how to do it.
To the Hinden-Peter!

18:12.324 --> 18:15.521
JOE: Oh, my God!
PETER: Joe, I am so sorry.

18:15.627 --> 18:17.595
How can you afford these things?

18:19.131 --> 18:20.120
[Answering machine beeping]

18:20.232 --> 18:23.724
Yeah, Cleveland, this is Quagmire.
Listen, I feel awful.

18:23.836 --> 18:25.326
Why don't you come on over and we can...

18:25.437 --> 18:27.302
try to get things back
to the way they used to be?

18:27.406 --> 18:28.430
Remember how it was?

18:28.540 --> 18:32.271
[In pseudo-Czech accent] Perhaps here
there are many unsuspecting foxes...

18:32.377 --> 18:34.072
to have sex with us.

18:34.179 --> 18:38.582
[In pseudo-Czech accent] That is why
we wear tight pants to show our bulges.

18:38.684 --> 18:42.518
- We are two wild and crazy guys!
- Two wild and crazy guys!

18:43.255 --> 18:44.586
You guys look stupid.

18:44.890 --> 18:46.949
Anyway, let's talk this thing through.

18:49.828 --> 18:52.092
Hey, Cleveland.
I was just leaving you a message.

18:52.197 --> 18:55.564
You violated the sanctity of my marriage.

19:09.348 --> 19:12.511
When the time comes, you'll know.

19:15.654 --> 19:16.643
QUAGMIRE: Damn it!

19:21.493 --> 19:22.960
This is awful!

19:23.061 --> 19:25.256
Somebody stop them! Do something!

19:29.268 --> 19:33.261
Good. Let the hate flow through you.

19:33.372 --> 19:34.896
You're not helping!

19:36.208 --> 19:38.301
I can't.

19:38.410 --> 19:41.379
It isn't in me to cause harm to anyone.

19:41.480 --> 19:44.415
No matter how much
someone has harmed me.

19:44.516 --> 19:46.313
I'm sorry, Cleveland.

19:46.585 --> 19:50.043
Cleveland, I think this beautiful woman
would like to say something to you.

19:50.155 --> 19:52.453
You told me this was Lois' intervention.

19:52.558 --> 19:57.427
- Nice. Cleveland?
- Loretta, what you did was unforgivable.

19:57.529 --> 20:01.090
- This marriage is over.
- Well, that's just fine, Cleveland.

20:01.200 --> 20:03.191
'Cause I am through being your wife.

20:03.302 --> 20:07.363
Well, I may not be perfect,
but I deserve better than you.

20:07.472 --> 20:08.564
Look at that, Lois.

20:08.674 --> 20:11.768
As beautiful as an HBO minority fairytale.

20:12.377 --> 20:14.436
But, Peter, their marriage is ending.

20:14.546 --> 20:15.979
Look at the bright side, Lois.

20:16.081 --> 20:19.050
It's a chance for a fresh start
for both Cleveland and...

20:19.318 --> 20:20.285
[Audience applauding]

20:20.652 --> 20:22.347
Oh, my God!

20:22.454 --> 20:23.716
What are you doing?

20:23.822 --> 20:26.154
- What's wrong with you?
- What the hell, man?

20:26.258 --> 20:27.748
- Hurts, doesn't it?
- What the hell... Yes!

20:27.859 --> 20:29.258
What the hell's your problem?

20:29.361 --> 20:31.329
- My friend? My friend?
- What?

20:31.430 --> 20:34.365
- You've been kicked in the...
- No way!

20:34.766 --> 20:37.894
- You're gonna be on TV.
- Oh, sweet!

20:38.003 --> 20:40.198
- Oh, my God.
- Wow! We love that show.

20:40.305 --> 20:42.671
- That is awesome. Hey, hi.
- You're on it.

20:42.774 --> 20:43.832
Oh, wow.

20:45.477 --> 20:50.210
Glenn, you sure you want to do this?
I already told you I forgive you.

20:50.315 --> 20:54.843
- No, I feel like I got off too easy.
- All right. If you insist.

20:54.953 --> 20:58.480
- You wanna ring the bell, Apollo?
- All right.

20:58.590 --> 21:00.217
Ding, ding.

21:06.298 --> 21:07.822
<i>[Theme from Rocky III playing]</i>

21:07.823 --> 22:08.823
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru